  "term": "external ear",
  "definition": "The external ear, in this packet’s context, is the dolphin’s outer ear canal and its surrounding fatty, vascular, and nerve-rich tissues. Together these structures help conduct sound and also appear to function as a complex somatosensory system adapted to underwater hearing and mechanosensation.",
